1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:06,738
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:18,182
Okay people, listen up.

3
00:00:18,182 --> 00:00:21,185
Today, we're talking about fermions.

4
00:00:21,185 --> 00:00:24,622
Fermions have a half-integer spin

5
00:00:24,622 --> 00:00:27,892
NOT a full-integer spin;
those are bosons.

6
00:00:28,926 --> 00:00:29,894
Where am I?

7
00:00:30,928 --> 00:00:32,196
Uh, hold on.

8
00:00:32,196 --> 00:00:34,932
I think we're going to have to
move to another room.

9
00:00:37,368 --> 00:00:41,039
Somebody's renovating this place, I guess.

10
00:00:41,706 --> 00:00:43,708
I'm so confused.

11
00:00:44,308 --> 00:00:45,610
My head hurts.

12
00:00:45,977 --> 00:00:47,779
Man, I'm sore all over.

13
00:00:47,779 --> 00:00:50,281
Feel like I got my ass kicked.

14
00:00:50,281 --> 00:00:52,383
Jesus Christ.

15
00:00:52,383 --> 00:00:54,485
What was I doing in there?

16
00:00:54,485 --> 00:00:56,621
How did I even get in here?

17
00:00:56,621 --> 00:00:58,222
I want a drink.

18
00:00:58,222 --> 00:01:01,426
It doesn't have to be bourbon;
I'm not too picky.

19
00:01:01,426 --> 00:01:04,362
You know, anything at least 80-proof.

20
00:01:04,362 --> 00:01:06,898
It smells like dog vomit in here.

21
00:01:06,898 --> 00:01:09,100
Oh, a hatch.  There's the answer.

22
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:11,502
Ohh, I don't know if I can reach it.

23
00:01:11,502 --> 00:01:13,471
I'll find a stick or something.

24
00:01:14,038 --> 00:01:16,407
What the hell did I do last night?

25
00:01:16,407 --> 00:01:20,645
I remember there was
some guy with an eye patch.

26
00:01:20,645 --> 00:01:21,779
And a midget.

27
00:01:21,779 --> 00:01:22,780
Oh, perfect.

28
00:01:22,780 --> 00:01:24,382
What were they talking about?

29
00:01:25,116 --> 00:01:25,917
[growls]

30
00:01:25,917 --> 00:01:29,587
And some sort of scam
involving corndogs.

31
00:01:29,587 --> 00:01:31,089
Shit, I don't remember.

32
00:01:31,789 --> 00:01:34,158
Ergh, can't reach.

33
00:01:34,158 --> 00:01:37,495
I can tell already this is
going to be a fun day.

34
00:01:38,162 --> 00:01:38,463
Rah!

35
00:01:39,263 --> 00:01:39,797
Come on!

36
00:01:40,598 --> 00:01:42,100
This sucks.

37
00:01:43,101 --> 00:01:44,936
[yawns]

38
00:01:44,936 --> 00:01:46,904
Seriously, how did I get here?

39
00:01:46,904 --> 00:01:49,507
I can't go through my
whole life living like this.

40
00:01:49,507 --> 00:01:50,475
Oh, drain.

41
00:01:50,475 --> 00:01:54,645
If I party this hard every night, I'm
going to end up dead in a few years.

42
00:01:54,645 --> 00:01:56,481
I don't remember what happened.

43
00:01:56,481 --> 00:01:59,250
I think I was watching
a movie about monsters...

44
00:01:59,250 --> 00:02:00,952
...and they attacked Canada?

45
00:02:00,952 --> 00:02:03,287
I mean, obviously, SOMETHING happened.

46
00:02:03,287 --> 00:02:06,390
I woke up in a trash compactor again.

47
00:02:06,390 --> 00:02:08,459
Yeah, this looks easier.

48
00:02:09,494 --> 00:02:14,132
Hey, the ruptured rusty rods reveal a rift!

49
00:02:14,999 --> 00:02:16,901
Whoa, wait, which way is up?

50
00:02:17,468 --> 00:02:19,570
Oh. Okay, that's cool.

51
00:02:19,570 --> 00:02:20,805
See?  An exit.

52
00:02:20,805 --> 00:02:24,208
I'm one of the kids who paid attention
to the hamsters in class.

53
00:02:25,076 --> 00:02:26,344
[coughs]

54
00:02:26,344 --> 00:02:29,413
Wow, this is not my finest hour, is it?

55
00:02:29,413 --> 00:02:31,616
Spending the night in the Dumpster,

56
00:02:31,616 --> 00:02:35,520
getting dumped out of a sewer pipe
facedown into a run-off puddle,

57
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:37,655
waking up in the afternoon,

58
00:02:37,655 --> 00:02:39,490
I'm probably missing work,

59
00:02:39,490 --> 00:02:41,526
I'm lost in the desert,

60
00:02:41,526 --> 00:02:45,496
I have many unexplained bruises
and facial lacerations...

61
00:02:45,496 --> 00:02:47,932
They say you know when
you hit rock bottom,

62
00:02:47,932 --> 00:02:51,235
but I can't say any of this
is completely unfamiliar.

63
00:02:51,235 --> 00:02:53,805
Except for being in the desert.
That's kind of new.

64
00:02:53,805 --> 00:02:56,774
The last time something like
this happened was Austria.

65
00:02:56,774 --> 00:03:00,178
Actually, Austria was even worse
because I woke up naked.

66
00:03:00,178 --> 00:03:02,246
I had to wander around lost in Innsbruck

67
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:04,782
until I could make some clothes
out of old garbage bags.

68
00:03:04,782 --> 00:03:07,318
[teleportation sound]

69
00:03:07,318 --> 00:03:09,720
Okay, well, this part's different.

70
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:11,122
Is this the only road?

71
00:03:11,989 --> 00:03:15,560
Eh...  God, that's a big cockroach.

72
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:16,027
[headcrab squeals]

73
00:03:16,027 --> 00:03:16,828
Jesus!
[headcrab squeals]

74
00:03:16,828 --> 00:03:19,230
That's the size of a friggin' softball.

75
00:03:19,664 --> 00:03:22,233
On second thought, I don't
think that is a cockroach.

76
00:03:22,233 --> 00:03:24,268
Looks like something
out of South America.

77
00:03:24,268 --> 00:03:26,971
I should start watching
National Geographic again.

78
00:03:26,971 --> 00:03:28,539
Oh, there's another one.

79
00:03:28,539 --> 00:03:30,141
I don't like the desert.

80
00:03:30,608 --> 00:03:31,375
Shit...

81
00:03:32,577 --> 00:03:33,611
[coughing]

82
00:03:33,611 --> 00:03:36,681
Someday, I'll be president
and it'll put this all in perspective.

83
00:03:36,681 --> 00:03:38,649
Oh! Shit!

84
00:03:38,649 --> 00:03:41,018
Somebody had a worse night than me.

85
00:03:41,018 --> 00:03:43,855
I'm not touching anything; I'm not going
to be part of the crime scene.

86
00:03:43,855 --> 00:03:47,024
That is rule number one
to staying out of prison.

87
00:03:47,024 --> 00:03:49,727
And to making proper measurements
on quantum particles.

88
00:03:49,727 --> 00:03:51,896
Man, I want to get back to the lab.

89
00:03:51,896 --> 00:03:54,899
No, wait, something happened
to it, didn't it?

90
00:03:54,899 --> 00:03:57,602
Huh.  A giant bung.

91
00:03:57,602 --> 00:04:00,137
I'm not seeing an entrance.

92
00:04:00,137 --> 00:04:03,441
Good God, I'm in the middle of nowhere.

93
00:04:03,441 --> 00:04:06,110
How did I get here? Am I a werewolf?

94
00:04:06,110 --> 00:04:08,112
Eh, butts.

95
00:04:08,112 --> 00:04:09,280
I'll go this way.

96
00:04:10,414 --> 00:04:12,049
Christ, it's hot out here.

97
00:04:12,049 --> 00:04:14,418
I caught a break being
passed out in the shade.

98
00:04:14,418 --> 00:04:16,420
Otherwise, my face would be sunburned.

99
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:20,324
It's always real classy going to parties
with half of your face burned red.

100
00:04:20,324 --> 00:04:23,461
This isn't the right way.
I should come down.

101
00:04:23,461 --> 00:04:24,962
Uh...

102
00:04:24,962 --> 00:04:25,997
Oh, that'll work.

103
00:04:25,997 --> 00:04:27,465
Okay...

104
00:04:28,299 --> 00:04:29,300
Not bad.

105
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:32,470
I could've gotten some
sick air if I had a pogo stick.

106
00:04:32,470 --> 00:04:34,272
And a jet pack.

107
00:04:34,272 --> 00:04:36,741
And... all right, I need to get out of here.

108
00:04:36,741 --> 00:04:40,044
Wandering lost in the desert
is not good for my career.

109
00:04:40,044 --> 00:04:41,712
Hey, what's this do?

110
00:04:41,712 --> 00:04:43,915
Oh, wow, it spins by itself.

111
00:04:43,915 --> 00:04:45,883
That...that's lazy.

112
00:04:45,883 --> 00:04:49,420
Power steering for when you're
too tired to turn a valve.

113
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:51,055
What's our obesity rate at?

114
00:04:51,055 --> 00:04:52,723
Isn't it like 30%?

115
00:04:52,723 --> 00:04:54,825
This is why I'm not in administration.

116
00:04:54,825 --> 00:04:56,827
I would've taken the
money for powered valves

117
00:04:56,827 --> 00:04:59,163
and used it to put a door
on the side of the building.

118
00:04:59,163 --> 00:05:00,731
Oh, hey, there's something down here.

119
00:05:00,731 --> 00:05:03,200
Lights and...
oh, there's the door!

120
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,569
Okay. I was confused.

121
00:05:05,569 --> 00:05:08,539
I have silly ideas about building design.

122
00:05:08,539 --> 00:05:10,207
Like, I wouldn't make people climb--

123
00:05:10,207 --> 00:05:12,476
Oh, hell. Maybe that's how that guy died.

124
00:05:12,476 --> 00:05:15,346
I should be careful...

125
00:05:15,346 --> 00:05:18,783
Yeah, maybe he was just stepping
outside the building for a smoke break,

126
00:05:18,816 --> 00:05:20,518
climbed the ladder up the silo,

127
00:05:20,518 --> 00:05:21,752
slipped at the top,

128
00:05:21,752 --> 00:05:23,387
then splat!

129
00:05:23,387 --> 00:05:25,122
I could be a detective.

130
00:05:25,122 --> 00:05:30,528
Although, as I say that, I still haven't
figured out what happened last night.

131
00:05:30,528 --> 00:05:34,432
I remember having problems.

132
00:05:34,432 --> 00:05:36,467
Lots of problems.

133
00:05:36,467 --> 00:05:38,302
I'm pretty sure about that.

134
00:05:38,302 --> 00:05:39,937
Ah, it's an elevator.

135
00:05:39,937 --> 00:05:42,573
Like something we might've
built in the Middle Ages.

136
00:05:42,573 --> 00:05:44,342
If we had motors...

137
00:05:44,342 --> 00:05:45,776
and water.

138
00:05:45,776 --> 00:05:48,846
All right, well, I think this was meant
to be operated by a second person,

139
00:05:48,846 --> 00:05:51,248
but if I double-time it, I should
be able to get up there.

140
00:05:51,248 --> 00:05:53,150
I wonder why it was designed this way.

141
00:05:53,150 --> 00:05:56,120
It was probably because of a union
contract that says that we have to hire

142
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:59,223
so many elevator workers
and this is to accommodate that.

143
00:05:59,223 --> 00:06:00,491
Da, dada, dada!

144
00:06:00,491 --> 00:06:02,326
Climb, climb, climb!

145
00:06:02,326 --> 00:06:03,327
Monkey madness!

146
00:06:03,327 --> 00:06:05,096
Gotta get up to get down!

147
00:06:05,096 --> 00:06:06,731
Whoo...

148
00:06:06,731 --> 00:06:07,865
Hurgh...

149
00:06:07,865 --> 00:06:10,034
Huh... well...

150
00:06:10,034 --> 00:06:13,037
I'm pretty sure that this
isn't the executive elevator.

151
00:06:13,037 --> 00:06:14,305
That would have carpeting.

152
00:06:15,673 --> 00:06:16,374
Oh.

153
00:06:16,907 --> 00:06:18,943
This is kind of a crappy entrance, huh?

154
00:06:19,343 --> 00:06:23,481
Oh well. I didn't see any rose petals
waiting for me on the outside.

155
00:06:24,081 --> 00:06:27,385
Still, with our budget,
this kind of bullshit.

156
00:06:27,385 --> 00:06:30,588
I think there's some class warfare
going on at this company.

157
00:06:31,455 --> 00:06:32,089
[gunshots]

158
00:06:32,089 --> 00:06:33,224
Whoa.

159
00:06:34,291 --> 00:06:35,493
[gunshots]

160
00:06:35,493 --> 00:06:37,528
What's going on in here?

161
00:06:37,528 --> 00:06:38,729
I've gotta check this out.

162
00:06:41,732 --> 00:06:44,935
I seem to remember
a lot of gunfire from yesterday.

163
00:06:44,935 --> 00:06:46,270
That's odd.

164
00:06:46,270 --> 00:06:47,805
Oh, he dropped his clip.

165
00:06:47,805 --> 00:06:49,774
I'll take it. Maybe I can
sell it back to him.

166
00:06:49,774 --> 00:06:51,475
I wonder how much I can get from him.

167
00:06:51,475 --> 00:06:52,810
Probably at least 20 bucks.

168
00:06:52,810 --> 00:06:53,744
[guard groans]

169
00:06:53,744 --> 00:06:54,311
[squish]

170
00:06:54,311 --> 00:06:58,215
Ugh! What's going on here?

171
00:06:58,215 --> 00:06:58,516
[squish]

172
00:06:58,516 --> 00:06:59,350
FUCK!

173
00:06:59,350 --> 00:07:02,853
Okay, something's not right here.

174
00:07:02,853 --> 00:07:06,157
This requires further investigation.

175
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:10,394
[squish]

176
00:07:10,961 --> 00:07:13,864
I'm not going to get
my 20 bucks from him, am I?

177
00:07:16,867 --> 00:07:19,000
[splat]

